t Values | `transform.shift_values` | Done | Lead/Lag values shift (K steps), DialogKit dialog with direction/step, SPS syntax, undo support |\n| Transform > Count Values within Cases | `transform.count_values` | Done | Count occurrences of values/ranges/sysmis across cases, DialogKit dialog & Values subdialog, SPSS COUNT syntax, undo support |\n| Transform > Create Dummy Variables | `transform.create_dummies` | Done | Indicator (0/1) binary variables generation (One-Hot Encoding), root name / prefix, reference category omission (k-1 dummies), DialogKit dialog, SPSSINC CREATE DUMMIES syntax, undo support |\n| Transform > Set Random Number Seed | `transform.random_seed` | Done | Global RNG state & thread-safe seed lifecycle, DialogKit dialog, SPSS SET SEED syntax, undo support |\n| Transform > Replace Missing Values | `transform.replace_missing` | Done | Imputation methods (Series Mean, Nearby Mean, Nearby Median, Linear Interpolation, Trend), DialogKit dialog with method selection & span, SPSS RMV syntax, undo support |\n| Transform > Create Time Series | `transform.create_time_series` | Done | Time series functions (DIFF, SDIFF, SMA, CSUM), DialogKit dialog with function & order/span settings, SPSS CREATE syntax, batch undo support |\n| Transform > Visual Binning | `transform.visual_binning` | Done | Continuous variable discretization (Equal Width, Equal Percentiles, Std Dev), DialogKit dialog & Make Cutpoints subdialog, auto/custom Value Labels, SPSS RECODE/VALUE LABELS syntax, undo support |\n| Transform > Optimal Binning | `transform.optimal_binning` | Done | Supervised discretization via Fayyad & Irani MDLP entropy optimization, max bins parameter, variable prefix, automatic Value Labels, DialogKit dialog, SPSS OPTIMAL BINNING syntax, undo support |\n| Transform > Rank Cases | `transform.rank_cases` | Done | Rank calculation with ties handling (Mean, Low, High, Sequential), direction (Ascending/Descending), types (Simple, Fractional, Percent, Ntiles, Normal: Blom, Tukey, Rankit, VW), DialogKit dialog & Types subdialog, SPSS RANK syntax, batch undo support |\n| Transform > Date and Time Wizard | `transform.date_time_wizard` | Done | Extract date parts (Year, Month, Day, Hour, Minute, Second, Day of week, Quarter), interval between two dates, duration summation/subtraction, DialogKit dialog, SPSS COMPUTE XDATE/DATEDIFF/DATESUM syntax, undo support |\n| Transform > Prepare Data for Modeling (ADP) | `transform.adp` | Done | Automated data preparation (screening, outlier winsorizing/sysmis, Z-Score/Min-Max rescaling, sparse category merge, MDLP binning, pairwise interactions, sample partitioning), DialogKit modal & subdialogs, SPSS ADP syntax, undo support |\n| Transform > Programmability Transformations | `transform.programmability` | Done | Multi-line transformation script engine (assignments, conditional IF/THEN/ELSE branching, vector math), DialogKit modal with quick snippets, live syntax validator, Output Viewer execution summary, BEGIN PROGRAM ... END PROGRAM syntax, undo support |\n| Analyze > Descriptive Statistics > Frequencies | `stat.frequencies` | Done | Frequency tables, percentiles, quartiles, DialogKit dialog & Statistics/Charts/Format/Style/Bootstrap subdialogs, `SET MTINDEX`/`BOOTSTRAP` SPSS syntax & bootstrap metrics (Bias, SE, Percentile/BCa CI), Vector-First Charts (Bar/Pie/Histogram with Normal curve) in Output Viewer & Pivot Tables, Format options (AVALUE/DVALUE/AFREQ/DFREQ, COMPARE/VARIABLE, LIMIT(n) table suppression) |\n| Analyze > Descriptive Statistics > Descriptives | `stat.descriptives` | Done | Mean, Sum, StdDev, Variance, Min, Max, Range, Skewness (+SE), Kurtosis (+SE), SE Mean, Z-scores (`/SAVE` + Undo), Display Order (`/SORT`), `/MISSING=VARIABLE|LISTWISE`, `Valid N (listwise)`, `TableStyleRule`, Dialog & Pivot Table, Bootstrap (`Percentile`/`BCa`, `Simple`/`Stratified`, `SET MTINDEX`/`BOOTSTRAP`) |\n| Analyze > Descriptive Statistics > Explore | `stat.explore` | Done | Exploratory Data Analysis, 5% Trimmed Mean, IQR, M-Estimators (Huber, Tukey, Hampel, Andrews), Percentiles (HAVERAGE & Tukey's Hinges), Shapiro-Wilk W (Royston 1992), Kolmogorov-Smirnov Lilliefors, 5 extreme values + `Label Cases by` (`/ID`), 4-row Levene Homogeneity of Variance & Spread-vs-Level power estimation, `MISSING=LISTWISE|PAIRWISE|REPORT`, Display (`Both`/`Statistics`/`Plots`), Vector Plots (Boxplot, Stem-and-Leaf, Histogram, Normal/Detrended Q-Q, Spread-vs-Level), Bootstrap (`Percentile`/`BCa`, `Simple`/`Stratified`), DialogKit subdialogs, `EXAMINE`/`EXPLORE` syntax |\n| Analyze > Descriptive Statistics > Crosstabs | `stat.crosstabs` | Done | Multi-layer contingency tables (`BY`), Pearson/Yates/LR/Fisher/Linear-by-Linear Chi-Square, Monte Carlo Patefield & Bounded Exact $r \\times c$, Nominal/Ordinal/Interval/Agreement/Risk/McNemar measures, Stratified $2 \\times 2 \\times K$ CMH/Breslow-Day/Tarone, Column Proportions $z$-test (+ Bonferroni), 3 residual types, 5 non-integer weight modes, full `CROSSTABS` `.sps` round-trip, DialogKit & Output Viewer |\n| Analyze > Descriptive Statistics > TURF Analysis | `stat.turf` | Done | Total Unduplicated Reach and Frequency (TURF) analysis, combinations 1..K, Reach count/%, Frequency count/%, Mean responses, Importance weights, Removal cycles, Advanced Selection (Heats), Reach & Frequency vector chart, Pivot Tables, TSV/HTML export, DialogKit dialog & subdialogs, SPSSINC TURF syntax |\n| Analyze > Compare Means > Means | `stat.means` | Done | Subgroup means breakdown, cell statistics (Mean, N, StdDev, Variance, Median, Min, Max), ANOVA table (Between, Within, Total), Measures of Association (Eta, Eta Squared), DialogKit dialog, SPSS TABLES BY syntax, Bootstrap (`Percentile`/`BCa`, `Simple`/`Stratified`) |\n| Analyze > Compare Means > One-Sample T Test | `stat.ttest.onesample` | Done | Student's One-Sample t-test, test value, df, p-value, mean diff, 95% CI, dialog & SPSS Pivot Tables, Bootstrap (`Percentile`/`BCa`, `Simple`/`Stratified`) |\n| Analyze > Compare Means > Independent-Samples T Test | `stat.ttest.indep` | Done | Independent-Samples t-test, Levene test (F, Sig), Student's t (equal var) & Welch's t (unequal var), df, p-value, 95% CI, Define Groups dialog & two-tier SPSS Pivot Tables, Bootstrap (`Percentile`/`BCa`, `Simple`/`Stratified`) |\n| Analyze > Compare Means > Paired-Samples T Test | `stat.ttest.paired` | Done | Paired-Samples t-test, Paired Descriptives (Mean, StdDev, SE), Pearson Correlation & Sig, Paired Differences (Mean, StdDev, SE, 95% CI, t, df, Sig), Paired Variables Dialog & 3 SPSS Pivot Tables, Bootstrap (`Percentile`/`BCa`, `Simple`/`Stratified`) |\n| Analyze > Compare Means > One-Way ANOVA | `stat.anova.oneway` | Done | One-Way ANOVA, Fisher's F-test, p-value via incomplete beta, Levene's test of homogeneity of variances, Descriptives with 95% CI, dialog & 3 authentic SPSS Pivot Tables, Bootstrap (`Percentile`/`BCa`, `Simple`/`Stratified`) |\n| Analyze > Correlate > Bivariate | `stat.correlations` | Done | Pearson r, Spearman rho, Kendall tau-b, 1-tailed / 2-tailed p-values, significance flags (* / **), cross-product deviations & covariances, pairwise/listwise missing handling, DialogKit dialog & authentic SPSS Pivot Tables, Bootstrap (`Percentile`/`BCa`, `Simple`/`Stratified`) |\n| Analyze > Nonparametric Tests > Two Independent Samples | `stat.npar.mann_whitney` | Done | Mann-Whitney U, Wilcoxon W, Z-statistic, Asymptotic 2-tailed p-value with tie adjustment, Define Groups subdialog, authentic Ranks and Test Statistics tables |\n| Analyze > Nonparametric Tests > K Independent Samples | `stat.npar.kruskal_wallis` | Done | Kruskal-Wallis H test, tie adjustment H_adj, df = k - 1, asymptotic p-value from chi-square distribution, Define Range subdialog (min/max), authentic SPSS Ranks and Test Statistics tables |\n| Analyze > Nonparametric Tests > Two Related Samples | `stat.npar.related2` | Done | Wilcoxon Signed-Rank Test & Sign Test, Z-statistic, Asymptotic & Exact 2-tailed 